          "file": "catalog/search/highlight.py",
          "claim": "WHAT: page_of computes `start = page * per_page` while its own docstring states `page` starts at 1, so a 1-based page number is treated as 0-based. WHY: page=1 returns results[20:40] instead of results[0:20], silently skipping the entire first page of results (and page=0 returns what should be page 1). HOW: subtract 1 before multiplying: `start = (page - 1) * per_page`.",
          "keep": true,
          "rationale": "The code at catalog/search/highlight.py:38-40 confirms the finding: the docstring states `page` \"starts at 1\", but line 39 computes `start = page * per_page`. For page=1 with default per_page=20, start=20, so results[0:20] (the entire first page) is silently skipped and results[20:40] is returned. This is a real off-by-one causing wrong results, not a style issue. No PreviousReviewDecisions entry addresses this page-slicing logic (index 1 concerns casefold offsets in highlight/snippet; index 2 concerns CSV escaping in an unrelated TS file), so it is not a repeat.",
